  "note": "Borough election polled Wednesday 20 May 1964 and declared the next day: three aldermen (for six years) and twelve councillors. Of the fifteen members of the new council fourteen were Unionists; Thomas Newell (Labour) beat Ralph O'Lone in the four-man contest for the three aldermanships. Percentage poll: 51.44 (aldermen), 65 (councillors). Labels from the report: Cooper (the Mayor) and Wright Unionists, O'Lone a former Unionist alderman."
